IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-definitions`
IMPORT `P5-section-5`
IMPORT `P5-art-43-annex-vi`
IMPORT `P5-art-47-48-annex-v`
IMPORT `P5-art-49-annex-viii-ix`

-- P5-tests-section-5-gap: the gap between Chapter III Section 5 (Articles 40 to 49, with Annexes V, VI, VIII and IX) and Chapter III Sections 1 to 3.
-- THE LITERAL READING (a marginal reading for a lawyer; NOTES.md, Marginal readings, M-1; the keel's fork F-113-groups, assumed, not mine to change).
-- Article 113 as amended gives one date to "this Regulation" in its second paragraph (2 August 2026) and carves out its Chapters, Articles and Annexes in the third paragraph (points (a) to (c)):
-- Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 (point (c)) apply from 2 December 2027 (systems of Annex III) or 2 August 2028 (systems of Annex I); Section 4 (point (b)) is dated too. NO point dates Section 5 (Articles 40 to 49).
-- So, read literally, Section 5 and its Annexes apply from the general date, 2 August 2026, while the Sections 1 to 3 that they serve do not yet apply to the same system.
-- The consequence shown below: on 1 September 2027 a provider of an Annex III system that is to be placed on the market on 3 December 2027 is already under Article 49(1) (register before placing on the market), Article 47 (draw up an
-- EU declaration of conformity stating that the system "meets the requirements set out in Section 2") and Article 43(2) (follow Annex VI, a procedure for "demonstrating the compliance ... with the requirements set out in Section 2"),
-- while the requirements of Section 2 themselves, as Article 113 dates them, are not yet in force. This file does not change the reading; it makes it visible. Nothing here says it is the intended law.
-- Art 111(2) is not the cause: a system placed on 3 December 2027 (after 2 December 2027) is not saved from either group; a system placed on 3 August 2028 (after 2 August 2028) is not saved from the Annex I date.

`Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` MEANS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`
`Art 40 to 49 tests Annex I route` MEANS `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I`

§ `One date, two groups`

-- args of the two keel-gate helpers: date asked, route, date placed, significantly changed
-- Annex III system placed on 3 December 2027, asked on 1 September 2027: Section 5 applies, Sections 1 to 3 do not.
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 40 to 49 Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE)
-- Annex I system placed on 3 August 2028, asked on 1 September 2027: the same gap.
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex I route` (Date 3 8 2028) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 40 to 49 Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex I route` (Date 3 8 2028) FALSE)
-- The boundary of the Annex III date (2 December 2027): the day before, the gap; on the day, both groups apply.
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 12 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 40 to 49 Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 12 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 2 12 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 2 12 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE
-- The boundary of the Annex I date (2 August 2028): the day before, the gap; on the day, both groups apply.
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2028) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex I route` (Date 3 8 2028) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 40 to 49 Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2028) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex I route` (Date 3 8 2028) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 2 8 2028) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex I route` (Date 3 8 2028) FALSE
-- Before the general date neither group applies (no gap): 1 August 2026.
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2026) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 40 to 49 Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2026) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE)

§ `The duties of this part that apply on 1 September 2027 while Sections 1 to 3 do not`

-- Article 43(2): a provider of a system of point 2 to 8 of Annex III follows the procedure of Annex VI (args: date asked, route, date placed, significantly changed, products covered by Section B of Annex I, Section B requirements integrated, point of Annex III).
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 43(2) the conformity assessment procedure the provider is to follow` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE 4 EQUALS JUST `Art 43 procedure of Annex VI (internal control)``; the function now takes the two Section B facts of Article 2(2) (seam S14) after the first four inputs, and FALSE and FALSE keep the meaning (no Section B products).
#ASSERT `Art 43(2) the conformity assessment procedure the provider is to follow` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE 4 EQUALS JUST `Art 43 procedure of Annex VI (internal control)`
-- Article 49(1): the provider registers before placing on the market (args: the four system facts, the two Section B facts, listed in Annex III, the point of Annex III).
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 49(1) the registration in the EU database is required` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE TRUE 4 EQUALS JUST TRUE`; the function now takes the two Section B facts of Article 2(2) (seam S14) after the first four inputs, and FALSE and FALSE keep the meaning (no Section B products).
#ASSERT `Art 49(1) the registration in the EU database is required` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 4 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Article 47(2): the EU declaration of conformity states that the system meets the requirements of Section 2 (args: the four system facts, the two Section B facts).
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 47(2) the declaration must state that the high-risk AI system concerned meets the requirements set out in Section 2` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE`; the function now takes the two Section B facts of Article 2(2) (seam S14) after the first four inputs, and FALSE and FALSE keep the meaning (no Section B products).
#ASSERT `Art 47(2) the declaration must state that the high-risk AI system concerned meets the requirements set out in Section 2` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same date, asked of an Annex I system placed on 3 August 2028 (Article 49(1) does not reach it: it is not listed in Annex III). Article 43(3): the provider follows the procedure the Section A legislation requires
-- (args: date asked, route, date placed, significantly changed, the two Section B facts, covered by the Section A legislation).
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 43(3) first subparagraph the conformity assessment procedure the provider is to follow` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex I route` (Date 3 8 2028) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `Art 43(3) procedure required by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I``; the function now takes the two Section B facts of Article 2(2) (seam S14) after the first four inputs, and FALSE and FALSE keep the meaning (no Section B products).
#ASSERT `Art 43(3) first subparagraph the conformity assessment procedure the provider is to follow` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex I route` (Date 3 8 2028) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `Art 43(3) procedure required by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 47(2) the declaration must state that the high-risk AI system concerned meets the requirements set out in Section 2` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex I route` (Date 3 8 2028) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE`; the function now takes the two Section B facts of Article 2(2) (seam S14) after the first four inputs, and FALSE and FALSE keep the meaning (no Section B products).
#ASSERT `Art 47(2) the declaration must state that the high-risk AI system concerned meets the requirements set out in Section 2` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex I route` (Date 3 8 2028) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Before the general date the same duties are NOT covered (NOTHING): the gap opens only on 2 August 2026.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 49(1) the registration in the EU database is required` (Date 1 8 2026) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE TRUE 4 EQUALS NOTHING`; the function now takes the two Section B facts of Article 2(2) (seam S14) after the first four inputs, and FALSE and FALSE keep the meaning (no Section B products).
#ASSERT `Art 49(1) the registration in the EU database is required` (Date 1 8 2026) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 4 EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 47(2) the declaration must state that the high-risk AI system concerned meets the requirements set out in Section 2` (Date 1 8 2026) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING`; the function now takes the two Section B facts of Article 2(2) (seam S14) after the first four inputs, and FALSE and FALSE keep the meaning (no Section B products).
#ASSERT `Art 47(2) the declaration must state that the high-risk AI system concerned meets the requirements set out in Section 2` (Date 1 8 2026) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The registration duty is also a clock: from 1 September 2027 the provider has 93 days to register before the placing on 3 December 2027 (a trace in P5-tests-art-49-annex-viii-ix.l4 reads BREACH after day 93).
